messages:
Sam: Heads-up: reproducible flake in Android sample using Retrofit suspend calls + an AuthInterceptor that does a blocking refresh. Repro: login -> rotate quickly -> call /me -> coroutine cancelled NPE in call adapter.

Priya: Oof. Which retrofit/okhttp versions and can you paste the interceptor + token refresh code?

Sam: retrofit 2.9.0, okhttp 4.11.0. Interceptor simplified:
```
class AuthInterceptor(val tokenProvider: TokenProvider): Interceptor {
  override fun intercept(chain: Interceptor.Chain): Response {
    val req = chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer ${tokenProvider.token}").build()
    val resp = chain.proceed(req)
    if (resp.code == 401) {
      // this was the mistake: blocking on main thread
      runBlocking { tokenProvider.refresh() }
      val retry = req.newBuilder().header("Authorization","Bearer ${tokenProvider.token}").build()
      return chain.proceed(retry)
    }
    return resp
  }
}
```

Sam: The runBlocking occasionally runs on the main thread during rotation; suspend-based Retrofit call adapters then see the call cancelled -> weird NPE in OkHttp's callback path.

Priya: Fixes: a) Do not block on the main thread from interceptors. b) Use OkHttp Authenticator for credential refresh (it runs on worker threads and returns a new Request) or c) pre-refresh tokens outside network layer so interceptor only attaches header.

Tom: Also watch suspend call adapters: they translate cancellation into call.cancel(), which can race with interceptor retries. Add a response-count guard in Authenticator to avoid retry storms. For samples, make TokenStore have a blocking refresh method backed by a background thread/lock and never touch UI.

CI-Bot: FYI flaky integration run: https://ci.redwood/infra/5678 flagged intermittent NPEs matching this pattern on Pixel 5 emulator.

Priya: I'll update the sample to switch to Authenticator + add a Robolectric test that simulates rotation + cancellation and assert no NPEs. Also will add a short note in devx README: "Don't runBlocking in interceptors; use Authenticator or pre-refresh tokens."

Sam: Thanks — will open PR with tests and sample changes.
